  "title": "Face Re-morphing and XSA-MAD for Morphing Attack Detection",
  "summary": "Face Re-morphing identifies differential morphing attack detection by leveraging feature-space similarity changes, while XSA-MAD uses CLIP-based semantic alignment to address unseen generation techniques in morphing attacks. Both methods demonstrate improved robustness and generalization across diverse morphing conditions.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Face Re-morphing uses feature-space similarity changes as a detection cue to identify morphing attacks.",
      "confidence": 0.95
